# Trivy vulnerability suppressions (auto-loaded by `trivy fs`).
#
# The Docker Engine CVEs below are false positives for crow.
# crow only imports the Docker API client and type packages
# (github.com/docker/docker/api/types/* and github.com/docker/docker/client)
# to talk to an external Docker daemon over its socket.
# It does not compile or run the Docker Engine / daemon code where these
# vulnerabilities live (plugin authorization, legacy plugins, etc.), so the
# vulnerable paths are never reachable from crow's binaries.
#
# They are also not fixable by a version bump: the fix is Docker Engine 29.3.1,
# but the github.com/docker/docker and github.com/moby/moby Go modules are
# deprecated and frozen at v28.5.2+incompatible and will never be tagged v29.
# The supported successor modules (github.com/moby/moby/client and
# github.com/moby/moby/api) are a ground-up API redesign still on a v0.x / beta
# line; migrating onto them is tracked separately and intentionally deferred.
#
# Refs:
#   https://github.com/docker/buildx/issues/3792   (v29 module path change)
#   https://github.com/moby/moby/discussions/52404  (docker/docker module deprecation)

# CVE-2026-34040 — Docker Engine daemon (plugin authorization)
CVE-2026-34040
# CVE-2026-41567 — Docker Engine daemon
CVE-2026-41567
# CVE-2026-42306 — Docker Engine daemon
CVE-2026-42306
# CVE-2026-33997 — Docker Engine daemon (legacy plugins)
CVE-2026-33997
# CVE-2026-41568 — Docker Engine daemon
CVE-2026-41568
